			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Introduce modular DevLog subsystem with OTLP tracing\n\nReplace ad-hoc logging in the IPC layer with a dedicated `DevLog` subsystem under `Source/IPC/DevLog/`. This module provides tag-gated console output, file sink mirroring, and fire-and-forget OTLP span exporting.\n\nKey components include:\n- `IsEnabled`/`IsShort`: Tag resolution logic supporting `Trace=all`, `Trace=short`, and specific tag lists.\n- `WriteToFile`: Lazy-initialized file sink writing to `~/Library/Application Support/land.editor.*.mountain/logs/<timestamp>/Mountain.dev.log`.\n- `AliasPath`: Replaces verbose Tauri app-data paths with `$APP` for readability in short mode.\n- `DedupState`/`FlushDedup`: Consecutive duplicate suppression to reduce log noise.\n- `EmitOTLPSpan`: Async HTTP POST implementation for OpenTelemetry data.\n- `IsBenignEnoent`: Filter for known-optional probe paths (VS Code/Copilot artifacts) to downgrade errors to debug logs.\n\nThe implementation follows strict PascalCase naming and explicit `::Fn()` qualification patterns, ensuring zero runtime cost in release builds via `cfg!(debug_assertions)` gating. The new `dev_log!` and `otel_span!` macros provide a unified interface for developers to instrument IPC handlers and boot sequences.",
			"SHA": "746075e9cc8ee101c809bb67f2628006eb4fa52b"
